    <item>
      <title>Unlucky Tourist - Jeff&amp;#039;s New Horizons Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/11/27/unlucky-tourist/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/11/27/unlucky-tourist/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 04:55:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-9791" class="post-9791 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Unlucky Tourist&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Last Sunday, Portia the dalmatian was camping at the campsite. I wouldn&amp;#8217;t mind having her around, but I did not invite her to move in this time.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/portia-camper-sm.jpg" alt="Portia, at the campsite: I needed a little escape, darling, so here I am on this island, getting in touch with nature and such." class="wp-image-9793" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Katrina told me that my luck with belongings will diminish. But I paid her a 10,000-bell purification fee and she sent me a zodiac sheep figurine (not one of her four lucky items). This will be the zodiac item for 2027, but I got it a bit early!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="578" height="371" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/zodiac-sheep.jpg" alt="The zodiac sheep figurine from Katrina." class="wp-image-9792" sizes="(max-width: 578px) 100vw, 578px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Yesterday was Thanksgiving, which meant that Franklin would be in town for the Turkey Day event.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/franklin2026-sm.jpg" alt="Franklin: I'm Franklin, professional chef extraordinaire. Nook Inc. hired me to come and cook for everyone." class="wp-image-9794" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Unlike some previous years, I came (mostly) prepared this time. I had almost all of the ingredients I would need already in storage. So it didn&amp;#8217;t take long for the cooking to begin.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/cooking2026-sm.jpg" alt="Franklin: Let's get cooking!" class="wp-image-9795" sizes="auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;The only exception was that I didn&amp;#8217;t have an olive flounder or scallop, so I had to do a little fishing and diving. But neither of them took more than a couple minutes. However, that did mean I had to decline Pascal&amp;#8217;s request for a scallop.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/pascal-no-wow-sm.jpg" alt="Pascal: It's cool, maaan. Scallops come and scallops go, but the sea will always be there." class="wp-image-9796" sizes="auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Interestingly, he did not give me any words of wisdom! So he only shares his wisdom if we give him scallops? That&amp;#8217;s kinda rude, and it doesn&amp;#8217;t seem like Pascal. In City Folk, he&amp;#8217;ll share his words of wisdom whether you give him a scallop or not!&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Anyway, these are the ingredients I needed for my four dishes:&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;ul class="wp-block-list"&gt; &lt;li&gt;clam chowder: 3 manila clams&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;pumpkin pie: orange pumpkin + white pumpkin&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;gratin: round mushroom + potato&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;meuniere: sea bass + olive flounder&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;And of course, I also added the secret ingredients to make the dishes even better:&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;ul class="wp-block-list"&gt; &lt;li&gt;clam chowder: scallop&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;pumpkin pie: green pumpkin + yellow pumpkin&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;gratin: dungeness crab&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;meuniere: barred knifejaw&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Here are my fully completed dishes:&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/dishes2026-sm.jpg" alt="Forest's villager celebrate the completion of the Turkey Day food." class="wp-image-9797" sizes="auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Lucky (the mummified/bandaged dog) was in town as a tourist, and he was present as I finished up the cooking segments. Sadly, he told me that he can&amp;#8217;t join in! He could only smell the food! I felt bad for him. I guess Lucky really is unlucky after all.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lucky-unlucky-sm.jpg" alt="Lucky: I can't join in since I'm a visitor, which is...tragic, honestly. But they can't stop me from smellin' the food!" class="wp-image-9798" sizes="auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Today, Isabelle announced Forest&amp;#8217;s first snowflakes of the season. Of course, they were just light flurries, and the snow won&amp;#8217;t stick to the ground until December 11th. But it&amp;#8217;s a sign that winter is just around the corner!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/isabelle-snow2026-sm.jpg" alt="Isabelle: And today we've had the first snow of the year! Winter has finally arrived, Forest!" class="wp-image-9799" sizes="auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I hope you all had a great Turkey Day, Thanksgiving, Harvest Festival&amp;#8230;or just a great day in general. I&amp;#8217;ll be back with another entry next week, and I hope to see you then!&lt;/p&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/11/27/unlucky-tourist/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-27T23:55:00-05:00"&gt;November 27, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-28T00:18:35-05:00"&gt;November 28, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/portia-camper-sm.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Marshmallow Yams - Jeff&amp;#039;s ACCF Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/11/26/marshmallow-yams/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/11/26/marshmallow-yams/</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:55:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-14279" class="post-14279 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Marshmallow Yams&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;As expected, I received Willow&amp;#8217;s goodbye letter in the mail today. So long, Willow!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8697-sm.jpg" alt="To: Jeff, I've decided to move away from Forest. It's hard to say bye to good friends like you. So I won't. Because I'm SURE we'll meet again somewhere! From: Willow" class="wp-image-14280" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;But her absence made this bulletin board post seem quite odd:&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8699-sm.jpg" alt="11/26/2026 ~Happy Birthday~ Today is Willow's birthday! Go congratulate her on another trip around the sun!" class="wp-image-14281" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;She still got a birthday notice on the bulletin board, even though she has already moved out! And yes, that was posted today! It wasn&amp;#8217;t an old note! I don&amp;#8217;t think I can congratulate her right now.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Anyway, today is Thanksgiving, which is the day of the Harvest Festival. I met up with Tortimer outside of town hall.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8698-sm.jpg" alt="Tortimer: Today we feast like kings! Today we gorge like pigs! Today we stuff ourselves like teddy bears!" class="wp-image-14282" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Tortimer handed me some silverware, and I began my search for Franklin. I first found him behind Guest&amp;#8217;s house (near Pac-Man Pond).&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8700-sm.jpg" alt="Franklin peeks out from behind Guest's house." class="wp-image-14283" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;He gave me a harvest clock for the fork and knife.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Peaches was getting hungry, and she said she&amp;#8217;d be mad if all that was left was side dishes&amp;#8230;but she didn&amp;#8217;t have to drag marshmallow yams like this.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8701-sm.jpg" alt="Peaches: I'd better head over there soon. I'll be so mad if all that's left is marshmallow yams and gourd surprise." class="wp-image-14284" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;First of all, how dare you. Put some respect on marshmallow yams! They&amp;#8217;re the best!&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Meanwhile, Nibbles was hoping a handsome boy would see her &amp;#8220;elegant cutlery moves&amp;#8221; and fall in love with her! Wow. Good luck with that.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8702-sm.jpg" alt="Nibbles: I'm hoping some handsome boy sees my elegant cutlery moves and totally falls for me, niblet!" class="wp-image-14285" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I continued taking silverware to Franklin as I found him around town.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8703-sm.jpg" alt="Franklin: Gobble!" class="wp-image-14286" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;And Big Top told me how the harvest festival is supposed to go down:&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8704-sm.jpg" alt="Big Top: First you stuff your face, then you complain about how full you are, then you go back for more!" class="wp-image-14287" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;But he got a little overexcited when I gave him a knife and fork. I&amp;#8217;m seriously hoping he was being sarcastic here, because this would be very sad otherwise:&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8705-sm.jpg" alt="Big Top: Whoo hoo! You got me a knife and fork?! I've...I've been waiting my whole life for this moment!" class="wp-image-14288" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;By the end of the night, I had collected eight pieces of the harvest set from Franklin. I sold them to Tom Nook for a total of 22,398 bells.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I hope you all had a great day! 🦃&lt;/p&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/11/26/marshmallow-yams/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-26T23:55:00-05:00"&gt;November 26, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-27T01:32:42-05:00"&gt;November 27, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8697-sm.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Harvest Festival 2026 - Jeff&amp;#039;s Animal Crossing Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/2026/11/26/harvest-festival-2026/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/2026/11/26/harvest-festival-2026/</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:45:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-6270" class="post-6270 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Harvest Festival 2026&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I received a goodbye letter from Gonzo in the mail today. That was fine by me, especially considering he was so rude last month.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ac-gonzo-out2026-sm.jpg" alt="Dear Jeff, Well, my streak continues... I just can't seem to settle down in any town for long. This is kind of odd, because I've said so many goodbyes, but this one actually hurts... Goodbye... -Gonzo" class="wp-image-6272" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I headed over to the wishing well, where the harvest festival was underway. I found Candi sitting across at Hank at one of the tables, and she wondered if she was a weirdo for liking apple pie as much as pumpkin pie. &lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ac-candi-pie-sm.jpg" alt="Candi: I like apple pies just as much as pumpkin pies. Does that make me a weirdo, sweetie?" class="wp-image-6273" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;No, of course not. That&amp;#8217;s not what makes you a weirdo.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;When I spoke with Genji, I noticed that he was holding his cup upside down!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ac-genji-upsidedown-sm.jpg" alt="Genji, holding his cup upside down: You have to eat a ton in order to build more muscle mass, with onion!" class="wp-image-6274" sizes="(max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;And then moments later, he would act like he was drinking out of it. But clearly there couldn&amp;#8217;t have been anything in it. 😆&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I swiped the fork and knife from the table and began my search for Franklin as I made my rounds. I first found him over by Ursala&amp;#8217;s house, and he gave me a harvest dresser for the silverware I swiped.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ac-franklin2026-sm.jpg" alt="Franklin: Yaaaaah!" class="wp-image-6275" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Back at the wishing well, Tortimer said he was thinking of having &amp;#8220;that new fellow&amp;#8221; over for dinner. I can see why Franklin is so scared. 😛&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ac-tort-fellow-sm.jpg" alt="Tortimer: I wonder what I should have for my main meal tonight? I'm thinking of inviting that new fellow over for dinner!" class="wp-image-6276" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I also met my newest neighbor (and Gonzo&amp;#8217;s replacement), Grizzly the grizzly bear. So one &amp;#8220;G&amp;#8221; named villager replaced another.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ac-grizzly2026-sm.jpg" alt="Grizzly: Hey! I haven't met you before, grrr...! I'd remember a face like that!" class="wp-image-6277" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;And of course, you can get free hints as to Franklin&amp;#8217;s location in this game. &lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ac-zoe-hint-sm.jpg" alt="Zoe: This is just between me and you, but I just saw this really suspicious guy in acre F, whiiifff." class="wp-image-6278" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;In case you&amp;#8217;re wondering why I call it a &amp;#8220;free&amp;#8221; hint: In City Folk, each hint costs you a set of silverware, so you&amp;#8217;ll have to backtrack to Tortimer to get more. That&amp;#8217;s kind of a pain. &lt;em&gt;This &lt;/em&gt;game handles the event much better. Plus it&amp;#8217;s kind of fun to swipe the silverware yourself instead of just having it handed to you. 😆&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I found Franklin a total of six times, earning six pieces of harvest furniture. Well, technically it was five pieces of furniture and one wallpaper. But I sold the six items for a total of 17,865 bells.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="450" height="346" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ac-franklin-junk-sm.jpg" alt="Franklin: Oh, it's just you. Why am I so delicious? I should've eaten more junk food when I was a chick." class="wp-image-6279" sizes="auto, (max-width: 450px) 100vw, 450px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I hope you all had a Happy Thanksgiving, Harvest Festival, Turkey Day&amp;#8230;or just a Thursday, depending on where you are and whether you played any Animal Crossing. 🦃&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;One other note: A few days ago, I posted my latest GameCube Moments video. Check it out if you haven&amp;#8217;t seen it yet!&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"&gt;&lt;div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper"&gt; &lt;iframe loading="lazy" title="Animal Crossing - GameCube Moments #31" width="660" height="371" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/M0nZrKHCy90?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/2026/11/26/harvest-festival-2026/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-26T23:45:00-05:00"&gt;November 26, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-27T00:24:45-05:00"&gt;November 27, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/acblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ac-gonzo-out2026-sm.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Uneven World - Jeff&amp;#039;s New Leaf Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/2026/11/24/uneven-world/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/2026/11/24/uneven-world/</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:33:35 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-18808" class="post-18808 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Uneven World&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Yesterday, Aurora told me she thought I could use a fish tee. That seemed like a bit of an odd thing to say, but I accepted the gift&amp;#8230;I even decided to wear the shirt.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261123_HNI_0082.jpg" alt="Aurora: Um, J-guy. I hope this isn't presumptuous, but I think you could use a fish tee." class="wp-image-18809" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Mira told me she was on an apple kick, and she demanded that I find her an apple!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261123_HNI_0086.jpg" alt="Mira: Get me an apple!" class="wp-image-18810" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I decided to be extra generous, and I gave her the perfect apple that I got from Mom in the mail last month. Mira loved it, and she rewarded me with an imperial wall.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261123_HNI_0089.jpg" alt="Mira: I gotta give you something nice in return, or the world will be uneven! Here! Have this!" class="wp-image-18814" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;It&amp;#8217;s going to be uneven regardless.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Today, Hornsby told me that he got a package that was supposed to have been delivered to Mira. I agreed to deliver it to its intended recipient.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261124_HNI_0092.jpg" alt="Mira: Huh?! This package was delivered to Hornsby's place?" class="wp-image-18815" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;There was a gray tartan shirt inside, and Mira said she ordered it to give it to me! She handed it back to me, but I didn&amp;#8217;t put it on. I&amp;#8217;ll wait until my new fish tee starts smelling before changing into something else. 😉&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I found Rasher the pig camping out at the campsite. I definitely was not interested in inviting him to town, not even for dinner. 😛&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261124_HNI_0097.jpg" alt="Rasher, at the campsite: The best part of camping is easily the food you get to eat!" class="wp-image-18811" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Saharah was also in town, and I paid her 3,000 bells to come home with me.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261124_HNI_0100.jpg" alt="Saharah walks into my house." class="wp-image-18812" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;She installed this library wall and pastel-dot rug in my house. I suppose they&amp;#8217;re not bad, but I did not keep them up.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261124_HNI_0002.jpg" alt="The library wall and pastel-dot rug that Saharah installed in my house." class="wp-image-18813" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/2026/11/24/uneven-world/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-24T23:33:35-05:00"&gt;November 24, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-24T23:33:36-05:00"&gt;November 24, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/20261123_HNI_0082.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Willow Wanders Away - Jeff&amp;#039;s ACCF Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/11/21/willow-wanders-away/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/11/21/willow-wanders-away/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:57:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-14269" class="post-14269 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Willow Wanders Away&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;As I started up the game this evening, I saw Chip outside of town hall. Oops, I missed another fishing tournament! But Chip told me that Nibbles won the black bass-only tourney with a 20.5-inch fish. Congrats, Nibbles!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8693-sm.jpg" alt="Chip: Nibbles from here in Forest! Fine fishing! A little finer than you, kiddo. Awful sorry!" class="wp-image-14270" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Speaking of Nibbles, I got to see the inside of her house today now that she has fully unpacked. Almost all of her furniture is on the right side of her house, with just a watermelon table on the left. I guess that&amp;#8217;s &lt;em&gt;one &lt;/em&gt;way to make sure you don&amp;#8217;t splash watermelon juice on all your furniture.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8694-sm.jpg" alt="The inside of Nibbles's house." class="wp-image-14271" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;Anyone who goes down that slide is going to slam into the wall.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;As I mentioned a while back, I gave Cube the catchphrase &amp;#8220;in a tray&amp;#8221; (referring to an ice cube tray). But tonight, he was talking about a tray of food in such a way that I almost didn&amp;#8217;t realize he was &lt;em&gt;also &lt;/em&gt;using his catchphrase in the next part.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="281" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/accf-cube-tray1.jpg" alt="Cube: Hmm. A lunchbox full of panna cotta and lemonade would be even cuter than a tray..." class="wp-image-14272" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;  &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="281" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/accf-cube-tray2.jpg" alt="Cube: But that would mean less panna cotta and lemonade, in a tray!" class="wp-image-14273" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;No, it would mean less in the lunchbox. 😉&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;My normal path around town is (roughly) counterclockwise, starting at my house and circling around town. So my last stop before reaching home is my next door neighbor Willow&amp;#8217;s house. I saw she was home, and a thought crossed my mind as I walked through her door: &amp;#8220;I hope she&amp;#8217;s not moving out.&amp;#8221; But sadly, that&amp;#8217;s exactly what I found. She is moving out, without notice. 🙁&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8695-sm.jpg" alt="Willow: Oh, look...it's twinkles, come to see me off! Wait, didn't I tell you?" class="wp-image-14274" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;She has grown on me a lot, and I&amp;#8217;m going to miss her. Most of my next-door neighbors in this game (when I have someone living in that spot) have been villagers I liked. It&amp;#8217;s sad to see her go.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I then left the game on for about 20 minutes as I waited for K.K. Slider to show up at the Roost (at 8 p.m.). Once he did, I asked him for a random song, and he performed K.K. Etude for me.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8696-sm.jpg" alt="K.K.: All right, get ready to dig the riffs on this ditty: K.K. Etude." class="wp-image-14275" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Earlier this week, I posted my annual slideshow of my best ACCF screenshots over the past year. Here is the 18th year in pictures:&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"&gt;&lt;div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper"&gt; &lt;iframe loading="lazy" title="ACCF - The 18th Year in Pictures (Animal Crossing: City Folk)" width="660" height="371" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/sDVIeyNaKjc?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/11/21/willow-wanders-away/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-21T23:57:00-05:00"&gt;November 21, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-22T02:55:58-05:00"&gt;November 22, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/RUU_8693-sm.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>A Ninja-Less World - Jeff&amp;#039;s ACWW Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/11/21/a-ninja-less-world/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/11/21/a-ninja-less-world/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:42:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-9131" class="post-9131 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;A Ninja-Less World&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	 	 	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Derwin pinged me behind town hall tonight, and he asked what I thought about his relationship with Angus. &lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/derwin-ship.jpg" alt="Derwin: Hey, gorgeous, what kind of relationship do you think Angus and I have?" class="wp-image-9132" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I guessed that they were &amp;#8220;archenemies,&amp;#8221; and I was apparently correct! He was so happy that I could see what was going on, he gave me a free common wall.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/derwin-bully.jpg" alt="Derwin: Yep! That's right! I mean, what a bully! I try to avoid that creep." class="wp-image-9133" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I later spoke to his archenemy Angus. He seemed disappointed that we live in a town with only one store and no pirate ninjas.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/angus-pirate.jpg" alt="Angus: There's only one store, nowhere to hang out, and not a pirate ninja in sight!" class="wp-image-9134" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;He gave me a free parquet floor, because it makes living in a ninja-less world easier to bear. I&amp;#8217;m not questioning the reasoning, but I&amp;#8217;ll gladly take a free gift.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/angus-ninja-less.jpg" alt="Angus: It makes living in a ninja-less world a little easier to bear." class="wp-image-9135" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Marina asked me to deliver a gift to Frobert, and that gift turned out to be a pep squad shirt. Frobert wasn&amp;#8217;t impressed, and he didn&amp;#8217;t put it on. I guess he didn&amp;#8217;t want to look like a cheerleader. 😆 When I returned to Marina, she gave me a round carpet for making the delivery.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;After I finished making my rounds, I went to the museum and down to the Roost. I let K.K. Slider play a random song for me, and he performed &amp;#8220;K.K. Soul.&amp;#8221;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/kk-112126.jpg" alt="K.K.: All right, get ready to dig the riffs on this ditty: K.K. Soul!" class="wp-image-9136" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;And last but not least, I have a bit of an announcement to make. For the first time in eight and a half years (since &lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2018/03/27/100-debt-free/"&gt;March 2018&lt;/a&gt;), I&amp;#8217;m changing the schedule of this blog. Instead of posting every week, I&amp;#8217;ll now be posting just twice a month. (The other Animal Crossing blogs are not affected by this change, so they will continue as normal.)&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;So there probably won&amp;#8217;t be a new entry next week, but I&amp;#8217;ll be back in December with more.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;img alt='' src='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0ff365ea4b4ae589e18c26b092fe26946a6e14116b63065f41029c8c6138c7c8?s=98&amp;d=mm&amp;r=g' class='avatar avatar-49 photo' height='49' width='49'/&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/11/21/a-ninja-less-world/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-11-21T23:42:00-05:00"&gt;November 21, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-11-22T01:36:14-05:00"&gt;November 22, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt; &lt;/article&gt;</description>
